@flexiarg problems/tension-proposes-candidates
@title Tension Proposes Candidates
@style pattern
@why war-room/wr-19-tension-must-generate-not-only-rank
@holds-at R6

@see-also futon-theory/reverse-morphogenesis
! conclusion: Add a tension proposer that creates candidate actions from tension instead of only reordering candidates supplied elsewhere.

  + context: Red ring at R6, ruling WR-19, established 2026-08-22 in
    p4ng/empirics-futon/wr-overlay.edn. No cascade mission supplies the
    mechanism, so this pattern has no supplier on its WIP card.
    + salience: 香. Observed, dated, and internal. WR-19's own record: on its
      first outing the War Machine exhausted its proposer-fed queue into
      learn-action-class before any outward open-mission surfaced — a system
      full of unresolved tension with nothing to do, because a tie-breaker
      cannot put an option on a menu it only reorders. Starvation is the felt
      signal; it was perceived before it was named.
    + caveat: the framing may be superseded. Earlier work on a metric over
      substrate-2 concluded that "morphogenesis" is a more useful way of
      thinking about where work needs to happen than "tension" (Joe,
      2026-08-25), and futon3/library/futon-theory/reverse-morphogenesis
      carries that method. This pattern is written in the vocabulary of the
      ruling it closes; whether the ruling itself wants restating is a separate
      question and is NOT settled here.
    + whose problem: the War Machine's own. The cost is borne inside the
      apparatus — a starved queue — and no outside party is worse off while it
      stands.

  + IF:
    The field contains tension that should generate a possible next action.

  + HOWEVER:
    The candidate space is ranked, not proposed, and the tension proposer is unbuilt.

  + THEN:
    Build a candidate source that reads the tension field and emits bounded candidate actions before ranking begins.

  + BECAUSE:
    Tension cannot generate action while it is only a weight over an already-existing menu.
    ?evidence(required): No source row demonstrates the unbuilt proposer emitting a candidate into the live candidate space.
